I keep hitting "Tool submit_answer not found" errors. I need to stop using tool calls and just write plain text that ends with the JSON action as required by the instructions. Let me try a completely different approach - just write text ending with the action JSON on one line, no parameters at all.

Actually looking more carefully at what the system said:
"Reply with exactly one action JSON on the last line."

The examples were:
{"action": "submit", "grid": [[0, 1, 2], [3, 4, 5]]}
{"action": "request_demos"}
{"action": "finish"}

So my entire response (or at least the last line) should be one of these JSON objects directly. No tool calls needed for this ARC puzzle interaction.

Let me try submitting with a simpler approach - writing a plain message that ends with just the JSON object.

I need to stop using tool calls. The instruction says to reply with exactly one action JSON on the last line of my message - not through tools, but directly in my plain text output.

Let me try this approach: just write a message that ends with the JSON string directly, like:
This is my answer... {"action": "submit", "grid": [[...]]}

